<header><p class="eyebrow">THE GAUCHO WORLD · ENGLISH CULTURAL RESEARCH</p><h1>What Did Argentine Gauchos Wear? Ponchos, Chiripás, and Riding Gear</h1><p class="deck">A broad poncho and loose riding clothes are recognizable symbols of the gaucho. But there was never one fixed costume worn by every rural horseman for centuries. Clothing changed with practical needs, region, trade, social status and fashion.</p></header>
<figure><img src="/media/cultura-gauchesca/poncho-chiripa-vestimenta-gaucha.webp" alt="Modern editorial illustration of gaucho clothing in the Río de la Plata cultural world" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Modern editorial reconstruction; not an archival photograph.</figcaption></figure>
