<section aria-label="Related historical guide"><h2>Historical context: what is a gaucho?</h2><p>The phrase <em>gaucho meaning</em> refers to a historical rural horseman, not simply a clothing style. To understand <em>what is a gaucho</em> before comparing garments across periods, consult our <a href="/en/what-is-a-gaucho/">historical guide to gaucho life and culture</a>.</p></section>
<section id="references"><h2>Sources and editorial method</h2><p>These notes expand the research and vocabulary of our Spanish cultural guide for an English-speaking audience. Historical claims, literary representations and modern editorial images are distinguished. External documents remain with their original custodians.</p><ul>{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target={s.url.startsWith('https:')?'_blank':undefined} rel={s.url.startsWith('https:')?'noopener noreferrer':undefined}>{s.name}</a></li>)}</ul>
